{
 "title": "Chapter 1: A Country With No Walls",
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Chapter 1: A Country With No Walls",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "s02b01",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Stand in Germany and look east.",
     "shot": "c1_lookeast",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b02",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "You won't find a mountain range or a desert.",
     "shot": "map:plain",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b03",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "You'll find the *North* *European* *Plain*, a vast flat stretch that runs,",
     "shot": "map:plain"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b04",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "with barely a hill in the way, all the way into the *heart* of Russia.",
     "shot": "map:plain"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b05",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Armies can cross it.",
     "shot": "c1_cross",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       4,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b06",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Traders can cross it.",
     "shot": "c1_cross",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "coins",
       "w:Traders",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b07",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "For a thousand years, *invaders* did.",
     "shot": "c1_cross",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "gallop",
       0,
       0.45
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b08",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In the 800s, the people who came were *Vikings*.",
     "shot": "c1_longship",
     "date": 862,
     "amb": "waves"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b09",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Instead of sailing west to England, many travelled east up Russia's rivers,",
     "shot": "map:rivers",
     "date": 862
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b10",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "chasing *silver* and the rich markets of Constantinople.",
     "shot": "map:rivers",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "coins",
       "w:silver",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b11",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "They became known as the *Rus*.",
     "shot": "c1_rus",
     "amb": "waves",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:Rus",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b12",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "According to an old chronicle, local tribes who were tired of fighting each other",
     "shot": "c1_tribes",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "boing",
       8,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b13",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "sent them an *invitation*.",
     "shot": "c1_tribes",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       "w:invitation",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b14",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Our land is *great* and *rich*, but there is no order in it.",
     "shot": "c1_letter",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "scribble",
       2,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b15",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Come and *rule* over us.",
     "shot": "c1_letter",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "scribble",
       2,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b16",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Historians debate how much of that story is true.",
     "shot": "c1_debate",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b17",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "But the name *stuck*.",
     "shot": "c1_debate",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "slam",
       "w:stuck",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "gag": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b18",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Rurik's descendants built a state around Kyiv, called *Kievan* *Rus*.",
     "shot": "map:kievanrus",
     "date": 900
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b19",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Russians, Ukrainians and Belarusians all claim it as part of their history.",
     "shot": "map:kievanrus"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b20",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In *988*, its prince, Vladimir, chose Orthodox Christianity from Constantinople.",
     "shot": "c1_baptism",
     "date": 988,
     "amb": "birds",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ding",
       "w:Orthodox",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b21",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "That tied Russia's religion, art, and politics to *Byzantium* for centuries.",
     "shot": "c1_byzantium"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b22",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Then, in the winter of 1237, the *Mongols* arrived.",
     "shot": "c1_mongols",
     "date": 1237,
     "amb": "wind",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "gallop",
       "w:Mongols",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b23",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "They came in winter on *purpose*.",
     "shot": "c1_mongols",
     "amb": "wind",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "gallop",
       0,
       0.45
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b24",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Frozen rivers became *highways* for their cavalry.",
     "shot": "c1_ice",
     "amb": "wind",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "gallop",
       0,
       0.55
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b25",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Russian cities fell one by one.",
     "shot": "c1_fall",
     "quiet": true,
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b26",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "In December 1240, they took *Kyiv*.",
     "shot": "c1_kyiv1240",
     "date": 1240,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b27",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "A European traveller passing through years later described fields still covered in bones and skulls.",
     "shot": "c1_traveller",
     "date": 1246,
     "quiet": true,
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b28",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The Mongols didn't just destroy. They *ruled*.",
     "shot": "c1_khan",
     "date": 1250,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:ruled",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b30",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Russian princes could keep their *thrones*, but only if they travelled to the Mongol",
     "shot": "c1_khan"
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b31",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "court, kneeled, and paid *tribute*.",
     "shot": "c1_khan",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "coins",
       "w:tribute",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02b32",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "And *one* *small* *town* learned to play that game better than anyone else.",
     "shot": "c1_moscow",
     "date": null,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:town",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02i01",
     "text": "So here's Moscow: a *tiny* wooden town, paying protection money to the Mongols.",
     "shot": "in_vault",
     "type": "STORY",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "whoosh",
       2,
       0.6
      ],
      [
       "thud",
       22,
       0.5
      ],
      [
       "coins",
       "w:money",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02i02",
     "text": "How does that end up owning more than a *tenth* of the planet?",
     "shot": "in_vault",
     "type": "STORY",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:planet",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s02i03",
     "text": "Short answer… a man nicknamed \"the *Moneybag*.\"",
     "shot": "in_vault",
     "type": "STORY",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "kaching",
       "w:Moneybag",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}